OL,3,GNEWSAChannel Islands facing 'hottest
OL,4,Aever summer'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe summer of 2026 is on course to be
OL,7,Fthe Channel Islands' hottest since
OL,8,Frecords began, according to local
OL,9,Fmeteorologists.
OL,11,FProvisional statistics from Jersey Met
OL,12,Fshow Jersey's average temperature,
OL,13,Fmeasured across both day and night, was
OL,14,F20.9C (69.6F) between 1 June and 15
OL,15,FAugust. That is 3.2C (5.8F) above the
OL,16,F1991 to 2020 average.
OL,18,FGuernsey's mean temperature over the
OL,19,Fsame period, and with two weeks of
OL,20,Fsummer to go, is 19.2B0C (66.56F), some
OL,21,F3C (5.4F) above the average,
OL,22,Fmeteorologists said.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
